Supply Chain"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be able to assess a company's environmental and sustainability performance:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Business / Facility","Environmental Data","Energy + Water + Waste","GHG Inventory","Compliance Assessment","ESG / Sustainability Gaps","Impact & Cost Analysis","Improvement Opportunities","Sustainability Roadmap","KPI Dashboard"]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should ideally graduate with one sustainability/environmental internship, strong environmental-engineering fundamentals, carbon-accounting knowledge, ESG fundamentals, Excel/Power BI skills, and at least one complete sustainability assessment project."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Tech/B.E. Environmental Engineering → Sustainability Consultant is a strong pathway into the expanding sustainability, ESG and environmental-services sector. The core employability combination is Environmental Engineering + Carbon Accounting + ESG + Environmental Compliance + Data Analytics + Business Consulting."},{"type":"p","text":"For stronger long-term growth, the student should avoid remaining limited to routine environmental monitoring. A better strategy is to specialize in ESG consulting, carbon and climate, environmental compliance, circular economy, sustainable supply chains, or sustainability analytics."},{"type":"p","text":"The most future-ready profile combines environmental engineering + sustainability strategy + analytics + technology, creating a progression from Environmental/Sustainability Analyst → Sustainability Consultant → Senior Consultant → Sustainability Manager → Sustainability/ESG Leadership."}]}]}